# LeakSanitizer suppressions for TaskSmack tests
#
# SDL3 is built as a static library (SDL_STATIC ON), so LSAN cannot match
# module names like "libSDL3". Suppressions must match function names instead.
#
# SDL_EGL_InitializeOffscreen allocates an EGL display and context that SDL3
# intentionally retains after SDL_Quit() for performance reasons (avoiding
# re-initialization overhead). LSAN reports this as leaked, but it is expected
# behavior in SDL3's cleanup model and not a TaskSmack bug.
leak:SDL_EGL_InitializeOffscreen

# Mesa's software GL driver (llvmpipe, under SDL's offscreen/EGL driver in CI) keeps small internal
# allocations it makes inside the first draw calls; LSAN reports them as indirect leaks with only
# driver frames (unsymbolized: the driver is unloaded by exit) below ImGui's OpenGL backend
# (tests/App/test_UiLayersOnDisplay.cpp, #1395). Matching the backend's draw function is the
# narrowest frame we own: ImGui_ImplOpenGL3_RenderDrawData allocates nothing itself per frame.
leak:ImGui_ImplOpenGL3_RenderDrawData

# The same driver keeps small internal allocations it makes while building a texture's mipmaps
# (glGenerateMipmap), again reported as indirect leaks under unsymbolized driver frames, so a module
# name (libgallium) can't match them. The test binaries load the real icons since #1954, so the title
# bar's icon texture reaches this path; the texture itself is released (UI::Texture deletes it).
# UI::loadTexture() calls glGenerateMipmap through a frame of its own that allocates nothing:
# suppressing loadTexture itself also hid any leak of its own, such as its decoded pixels (#2166).
leak:generateBoundTextureMipmaps
